Migrate my Nix-managed pi-herdr-subagents configuration from inline JSON roles to the new Markdown role catalogue.

   Required target layout:

   ~/.pi/agent/herdr-subagents.json
   ~/.pi/agent/herdr-subagents/roles/<role-name>.md

   Make these changes in the Nix source that manages those files:

   1. Keep only `orchestrator` and `defaults` in `herdr-subagents.json`.
   2. Remove the JSON `roles` property completely.
   3. Create one managed Markdown file per existing role at:
      `.pi/agent/herdr-subagents/roles/<role-name>.md`
   4. For each role document:
      - derive the role name from the filename;
      - put optional `description`, `model`, and `thinking` fields in YAML frontmatter;
      - put the former `prompt` value in the Markdown body;
      - preserve prompt wording, paragraphs, lists, and internal whitespace;
      - ensure the body is non-empty.
   5. Prefer readable Nix multiline strings instead of escaped JSON prompt strings.
   6. Preserve all existing role metadata and model candidate ordering exactly.
   7. Do not introduce project-local catalogues, nesting, inheritance, or templating.
   8. Update any comments or documentation in the Nix configuration that still describes inline JSON roles.

   Example Nix shape:

   home.file.".pi/agent/herdr-subagents.json".text = builtins.toJSON {
     orchestrator.enabled = false;
     defaults = {
       model = [
         "provider/model-a"
         "provider/model-b"
       ];
       thinking = "medium";
     };
   };

   home.file.".pi/agent/herdr-subagents/roles/explore.md".text = ''
     ---
     description: Read-only repository exploration
     model:
       - provider/model-a
       - provider/model-b
     thinking: low
     ---

     Act as a read-only repository investigator.

     Preserve the complete existing prompt here.
   '';

   Inspect the repository first and match its existing Nix/Home Manager conventions. Make only migration-related changes.

   Verify by:
   - running the repository’s normal Nix formatting and checks;
   - building or evaluating the affected Home Manager configuration;
   - confirming the generated JSON has no `roles` property;
   - confirming every generated role document has valid YAML frontmatter and a non-empty body.

   Report the changed files, migrated role names, and verification results. Remind me to run `/reload` in Pi after applying the configuration.

